WHAT: Moves bounds checking from per-word reads to dispatch level for all
fixed-size ABI type decodes. Individual read_word calls use unchecked access;
a single upfront check validates total calldata length.

WHY: Fe's Decode impls for u256, address, bool etc. each called read_word
with individual bounds checks. For a function with 3 parameters, that's 3
redundant bounds checks when one upfront check suffices. This eliminates
uaddo/branch per parameter decode.

GAS IMPACT: -6197 gas total. ALL 17 benchmarked functions improved.
  math: -625 each (3 functions, -9.1% to -9.9%)
  governance/vote: -525
  verifier/plonkVerify: -966
  amm/addLiquidity: -452
  erc20: -200 to -400
  governance: -30 to -357
  verifier/groth16Verify: -259
  amm: -69 to -276

CODEGEN IMPACT: Significant reduction in uaddo count across all contracts.
Branch count drops as overflow check branches are eliminated.

TEAM NOTES: Third Fe std library unchecked change. Steps 15, 16, 18 together
saved ~9,800 gas. The pattern is consistent: identify provably-safe arithmetic
in hot paths, add #[arithmetic(unchecked)]. This step moved from individual
unchecked annotations to a structural change (one check, many unchecked reads).
